WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.867
This skull has a normal bite. The big upper and lower back teeth meet in line.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:09.210
Here the lower jaw sits too far back. Braces can move teeth,

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.509
but not the jaw bones.

00:00:11.309 --> 00:00:15.960
The surgeon splits the lower jaw from inside your mouth and slides the front part forward.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.806
Small titanium plates hold it while it heals.

00:00:19.606 --> 00:00:21.953
Here the lower jaw sits too far forward.

00:00:22.753 --> 00:00:24.694
The surgeon may move both jaws.

00:00:25.044 --> 00:00:29.716
About 10 in 100 people have a numb lip or chin for several weeks after surgery.
